      "sourceHash": "6a55eff77e46489fc48b5859d9607a33d5dad610ca2dc496c1376189b524f39e",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.22,
          "end": 5.37,
          "en": "-: You can simply Google for Firebase auth REST API",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 5.37,
          "end": 6.78,
          "en": "and you should find an article",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.78,
          "end": 9.409,
          "en": "in the official docs which gives you an overview",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 9.409,
          "end": 12.93,
          "en": "over the REST endpoints Firebase offers to you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 12.93,
          "end": 16.657,
          "en": "for creating users and logging users in.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 16.657,
          "end": 18.9,
          "en": "here on the right you see the different things you can do",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 18.9,
          "end": 23.55,
          "en": "with that backend, with that REST API Firebase offers you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 23.55,
          "end": 25.95,
          "en": "It's a different REST API than we used before.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 25.95,
          "end": 29.46,
          "en": "It's not our database REST API we created automatically.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 29.46,
          "end": 33.45,
          "en": "It's a dedicated authentication API offered by Firebase",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 33.45,
          "end": 37.14,
          "en": "and we need only two methods, signing users up with email",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 37.14,
          "end": 40.98,
          "en": "and password and signing users in with email and password.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 40.98,
          "end": 43.2,
          "en": "So of course let's start with signing users up",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 43.2,
          "end": 46.98,
          "en": "because we can't sign in if we have no users, right?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 46.98,
          "end": 51.03,
          "en": "This is the URL to which you need to send your request.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 51.03,
          "end": 53.73,
          "en": "So this is the URL we'll have to send the request to",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 53.73,
          "end": 56.88,
          "en": "with this data, with the email, password,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 56.88,
          "end": 59.13,
          "en": "And then this returnSecureToken thing",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 59.13,
          "end": 61.86,
          "en": "which we also have to add to our request body",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 61.86,
          "end": 64.59,
          "en": "which is a boolean that essentially should always be true.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 64.59,
          "end": 66.21,
          "en": "Firebase just needs that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 66.21,
          "end": 69.84,
          "en": "you can ignore that your API might not need that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 69.84,
          "end": 73.44,
          "en": "Now we'll get back a response with, for example",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 73.44,
          "end": 76.8,
          "en": "the email address, the ID of the user,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 76.8,
          "end": 79.74,
          "en": "because Firebase automatically creates a new unique ID",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 79.74,
          "end": 80.91,
          "en": "for each user.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 80.91,
          "end": 83.37,
          "en": "And we also get back that ID token",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 83.37,
          "end": 86.43,
          "en": "which is that token I mentioned on the slide earlier.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 86.43,
          "end": 88.92,
          "en": "So Firebase already gives us such a token",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 88.92,
          "end": 90.24,
          "en": "once we sign a user up.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 90.24,
          "end": 92.1,
          "en": "We don't even need to sign in thereafter,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 92.1,
          "end": 95.16,
          "en": "we automatically get the token when a user signed up",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 95.16,
          "end": 97.08,
          "en": "we also get expiresIn field,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 97.08,
          "end": 99.78,
          "en": "which tells us how long that token will be valid",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 99.78,
          "end": 103.44,
          "en": "because for security reasons, these tokens will expire.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 103.44,
          "end": 104.78999999999999,
          "en": "For Firebase for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 104.78999999999999,
          "end": 107.52000000000001,
          "en": "they at the moment expire after one hour",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 107.52000000000001,
          "end": 109.68,
          "en": "Thereafter, you either have to refresh them,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 109.68,
          "end": 113.25200000000001,
          "en": "which we'll not cover here, or log in again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 113.25200000000001,
          "end": 117.6,
          "en": "Back to this URL though, we need to send this request",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 117.6,
          "end": 121.8,
          "en": "and that screen's for a new service here that actually deals",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 121.8,
          "end": 123.57,
          "en": "with that request sending.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 123.57,
          "end": 127.41,
          "en": "So in the auth folder, I'll add my authservice.ts file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 127.41,
          "end": 131.73,
          "en": "which is a service that will be responsible",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 131.73,
          "end": 134.49,
          "en": "for signing users up, signing users in,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 134.49,
          "end": 136.987,
          "en": "and managing that token of my user.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 136.987,
          "end": 139.38,
          "en": "In that auth service file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 139.38,
          "end": 142.57,
          "en": "let's say for export class AuthService and that service",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 144.72,
          "end": 149.34,
          "en": "will receive the @injectable decorator, which is imported",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 149.34,
          "end": 152.46,
          "en": "from @angular core, where I will use that shortcut",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 152.46,
          "end": 155.37,
          "en": "for providing it by setting provided into root.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 155.37,
          "end": 157.77,
          "en": "In that object we can pass to injectable.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 157.77,
          "end": 160.11,
          "en": "The alternative would be to add it to the provider's",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 160.11,
          "end": 162.32999999999998,
          "en": "array of the app module.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 162.32999999999998,
          "end": 165.57,
          "en": "Now in that auth service, we can of course start relatively",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 165.57,
          "end": 168.69,
          "en": "simple by adding one method, a signup method",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 168.69,
          "end": 171.18,
          "en": "and this method should do just what the name suggests.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 171.18,
          "end": 172.65,
          "en": "It should sign the user up,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 172.65,
          "end": 175.563,
          "en": "it should send the request to that signup URL.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 176.76,
          "end": 181.08,
          "en": "Therefore, we will need the angular HTTP client, of course",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 181.08,
          "end": 182.52,
          "en": "and this needs to be injected.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 182.52,
          "end": 184.29,
          "en": "So let's add the constructor",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 184.29,
          "end": 186.96,
          "en": "and now make sure you got @injectable here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 186.96,
          "end": 189.75,
          "en": "Even if you provided the service in the providers array",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 189.75,
          "end": 192.6,
          "en": "of the app module, as soon as you inject the service",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 192.6,
          "end": 194.82,
          "en": "into a service you need @injectable,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 194.82,
          "end": 197.31,
          "en": "not necessarily with that object being passed to it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 197.31,
          "end": 200.043,
          "en": "but you need the @injectable decorator itself.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 200.88,
          "end": 204.18,
          "en": "And now we can inject the HTTP client",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 204.18,
          "end": 207.3,
          "en": "which I'll store in a private property named HTTP,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 207.3,
          "end": 209.43,
          "en": "and a type will be HTTP client",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 209.43,
          "end": 214.161,
          "en": "and it's imported from @angular/comment/HTTP.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 214.161,
          "end": 215.19,
          "en": "In the signup method,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 215.19,
          "end": 218.25,
          "en": "we can now use the HTTP client to send a-",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 218.25,
          "end": 222.66,
          "en": "Let's have a look at documentation, post request here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 222.66,
          "end": 224.76,
          "en": "Send a post request to that URL,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 224.76,
          "end": 229.29,
          "en": "so copy that URL here, and here we'll use the post method",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 229.29,
          "end": 232.77,
          "en": "and then send a request to this URL.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 232.77,
          "end": 236.28,
          "en": "Now please note that in this URL we got that API key thing",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 236.28,
          "end": 239.04,
          "en": "which in the end is just something you have to replace",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 239.04,
          "end": 241.5,
          "en": "with your Firebase API key.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 241.5,
          "end": 243.99,
          "en": "And you can find that Firebase API key",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 243.99,
          "end": 246.54,
          "en": "in your Firebase web console and there",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 246.54,
          "end": 250.02,
          "en": "by clicking on that gear icon under project settings.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 250.02,
          "end": 252.96,
          "en": "And then it's this API key here, which you need.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 252.96,
          "end": 254.66,
          "en": "You can simply copy and paste that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 256.08,
          "end": 258.69,
          "en": "and then replace API key here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 258.69,
          "end": 261.993,
          "en": "including the square brackets with that copied key.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 264.21,
          "end": 267.15,
          "en": "This is the URL we have to send a request to.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 267.15,
          "end": 268.53,
          "en": "Now since the post request,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 268.53,
          "end": 270.99,
          "en": "we of course also need to attach some data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 270.99,
          "end": 273.33,
          "en": "So let me attach a JavaScript object here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 273.33,
          "end": 276.69,
          "en": "and that JavaScript object should hold three properties.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 276.69,
          "end": 279.51,
          "en": "The three properties this endpoint expects,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 279.51,
          "end": 282.96,
          "en": "email, password, and returnSecureToken.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 282.96,
          "end": 286.35,
          "en": "These are the three data pieces this backend endpoint",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 286.35,
          "end": 289.29,
          "en": "requires, and therefore I'll send my email here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 289.29,
          "end": 292.29,
          "en": "and I do expect to get that here as a string.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 292.29,
          "end": 295.14,
          "en": "I also expect to get the password as a string.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 295.14,
          "end": 296.67,
          "en": "So I will send the email here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 296.67,
          "end": 299.55,
          "en": "Email key gets the email value here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 299.55,
          "end": 301.26,
          "en": "and then the same for the password.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 301.26,
          "end": 304.02,
          "en": "Password key gets that password value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 304.02,
          "end": 306.42,
          "en": "The values here are, the arguments I'm getting,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 306.42,
          "end": 308.13,
          "en": "you could name these differently.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 308.13,
          "end": 310.59,
          "en": "Email and password have to be named like this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 310.59,
          "end": 313.891,
          "en": "because our API expects exactly these keys.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 313.891,
          "end": 316.47,
          "en": "It always expects a returnSecureToken.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 316.47,
          "end": 318.57,
          "en": "So you must set this as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 318.57,
          "end": 320.67,
          "en": "And as you can learn in the official docs",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 320.67,
          "end": 322.38,
          "en": "this should always be true.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 322.38,
          "end": 325.26,
          "en": "So they offer, let's simply set this to true here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 325.26,
          "end": 326.52,
          "en": "Perfect.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 326.52,
          "end": 329.34,
          "en": "So this now will send an HTTP request",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 329.34,
          "end": 331.803,
          "en": "to that backend here to this URL.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 333.99,
          "end": 337.56,
          "en": "As you learned, the HTTP client does nothing",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 337.56,
          "end": 339.96,
          "en": "without someone subscribing though, and we're not",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 339.96,
          "end": 342.57,
          "en": "even calling the signup method anyways.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 342.57,
          "end": 345.543,
          "en": "So let's return this prepared observable now so",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 345.543,
          "end": 348.72,
          "en": "that we can subscribe in the auth component, which is where",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 348.72,
          "end": 351.84000000000003,
          "en": "we might also be interested in getting the response of that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 351.84000000000003,
          "end": 353.466,
          "en": "because if we get an error, we probably",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 353.466,
          "end": 356.49,
          "en": "wanna display an error message and whilst we're",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 356.49,
          "end": 357.78,
          "en": "waiting for the response,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 357.78,
          "end": 360.21,
          "en": "we might want to show some loading indicator.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 360.21,
          "end": 362.43,
          "en": "So therefore returning the observable such",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 362.43,
          "end": 364.77,
          "en": "that we know the current state of the request",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 364.77,
          "end": 367.293,
          "en": "in the auth component makes a lot of sense.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 368.784,
          "end": 372.63,
          "en": "We also can define the format of the data we'll get back",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 372.63,
          "end": 376.05,
          "en": "because we will get back these six fields here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 376.05,
          "end": 380.478,
          "en": "and therefore I will create a new interface actually here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 380.478,
          "end": 382.83,
          "en": "in the auth service because I only need it in here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
